<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
  The Psync mark ("Engraved Halves") as the adaptive icon's foreground.

  Geometry: the two half-discs are the path data of assets/psync-logo.svg, verbatim, in its
  1024 x 1024 space; the group below scales that space into the 108dp adaptive canvas and keeps
  (512, 512) on the centre (54 = 512 x 0.072 + 17.136). The mark's farthest point is then 26.2dp
  from the centre, inside the 33dp radius of the 66dp safe zone that every launcher mask keeps.

  The grooves: the SVGs paint them as a 72-wide round-capped stroke in the ground colour (or use
  that stroke as a mask). A VectorDrawable has no mask, and the monochrome layer has no ground
  colour to paint with, so here each groove is a real HOLE: the sub-path after the first Z. It is
  wound counter-clockwise against the half's clockwise outline, so the default non-zero fill cuts
  it out (android:fillType is API 24+, and is not needed). Each round cap is two quarter arcs
  through its tip. ic_launcher_monochrome.xml, splash_mark.xml and (without the holes)
  ic_stat_psync.xml carry the same two paths: change one, change all four.

  The colours are literal on purpose: a launcher may run in night mode, and a night-qualified
  colour would turn the ink pale on the pale icon ground (@color/ic_launcher_background).
-->
